llm-mini-infer's image: third-party notices
===========================================

This image holds llm-mini-infer, under the Apache License 2.0 (its LICENSE is in
site-packages/llm_mini_infer-*.dist-info/licenses/), and third-party software, each under its own licence, which the
image keeps where its package installs it. Here site-packages is /opt/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages.


NVIDIA

The base image (the label org.opencontainers.image.base.name) is NVIDIA's, under the NVIDIA Deep Learning Container
License: /NGC-DL-CONTAINER-LICENSE. This image is built on it and adds llm-mini-infer and its dependencies; NVIDIA does
not endorse it. The CUDA libraries in the nvidia-* wheels, the copies other wheels bundle, the NVIDIA tools some wheels
carry beside them (Triton's ptxas and disassemblers, CUPTI's profiler libraries) and CuTe DSL (the nvidia-cutlass-dsl
wheels, which FlashInfer uses) are under the licence of the wheel that carries each.


CUTLASS

llm-mini-infer's FP8 GEMM library (/opt/llm-mini-infer/kernels/) is compiled from CUTLASS's headers, so it contains
CUTLASS code: BSD-3-Clause, its text at the end of site-packages/llm_mini_infer-*.dist-info/licenses/LICENSE.


Python distributions (/opt/venv)

site-packages/*.dist-info/ names each distribution with its version and holds its licence files (nvidia-cusparselt-cu13
keeps its own at site-packages/nvidia/cusparselt/LICENSE.txt). The wheels that carry no licence file:
- cuda-toolkit: NVIDIA's CUDA Toolkit meta-package, which installs nothing but its metadata: the CUDA Toolkit's
  licence, site-packages/nvidia_cuda_runtime-*.dist-info/licenses/License.txt
- flashinfer-jit-cache, flashinfer-jit-cache-sm120f: FlashInfer's AOT modules, under FlashInfer's licence (Apache-2.0),
  site-packages/flashinfer_python-*.dist-info/licenses/LICENSE
- nvidia-ml-py: BSD-3-Clause, as the header of site-packages/pynvml.py states it
- tokenizers: Apache-2.0, as its metadata's classifier states (the text: llm-mini-infer's LICENSE); its SBOM,
  site-packages/tokenizers-*.dist-info/sboms/, lists the Rust crates compiled into it and their licences

Pillow's wheel bundles the libraries it reads and writes images with (site-packages/pillow.libs/), under their
projects' licences, which Pillow's licence file reproduces a section each
(site-packages/pillow-*.dist-info/licenses/LICENSE):
- libjpeg: Pillow's LIBJPEG
- libpng16: Pillow's LIBPNG
- libwebp, libwebpdemux, libwebpmux, libsharpyuv: Pillow's LIBWEBP
- libtiff: Pillow's LIBTIFF
- libopenjp2: Pillow's OPENJPEG
- libavif: Pillow's LIBAVIF
- liblcms2: Pillow's LCMS2
- libfreetype: Pillow's FREETYPE2
- libharfbuzz: Pillow's HARFBUZZ
- libbrotlicommon, libbrotlidec: Pillow's BROTLI
- liblzma: Pillow's LIBLZMA
- libzstd: Pillow's ZSTD
- libxcb: Pillow's XCB
- libXau: Pillow's XAU


apt packages (Ubuntu 24.04, and the base image's CUDA packages)

`dpkg -l` lists them, and each one's copyright file is /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright; NVIDIA's CUDA packages,
which have none, are under the CUDA Toolkit's licence and the container licence (above). Their sources, the GPL and
LGPL packages' among them, are in Ubuntu's archive as https://snapshot.ubuntu.com keeps it: this image's packages at
the snapshot /etc/apt/sources.list.d/ubuntu.sources names, the base image's own at a snapshot of a time its version
was current. With that snapshot as a deb-src source: apt-get source <source package>=<version>.
